    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Description\n\nWhen `MiniGit.show_at_cursor` is called inside a `minigit://*` buffer and makes it to the \"show range history\" section of the code, the `cwd` argument to `H.git_cli_output` in [the definition of `is_in_git`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/42a58673bc86359b006f83fecd971ecb95ee8bf8/lua/mini/git.lua#L333-L335) is `\"minigit://n\"` (where `n` is a number).\r\n\r\nThis ends up making the git command hang until `config.job.timeout` milliseconds have elapsed, when an error is raised (by default, this is 30 seconds).\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `:lua require(\"mini.git\").setup()`\r\n1. `:Git show`\r\n1. `:lua MiniGit.show_at_cursor()`\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n1. The UI doesn't block\r\n1. A message saying \"Nothing Git-related to show at cursor\" (or similar) is displayed\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe UI blocks for 30 seconds. It can be recovered with `ctrl-c`, but then 30 seconds later an error message will still be displayed.",
